      <MissionDesc>COHERENT DEVELOPMENT RESEARCH INSTITUTE (CDRI) IS A NOT-FOR-PROFIT ORGANIZATION DEDICATED TO THE GENERATION, APPLICATION, AND DIFFUSION OF KNOWLEDGE THAT WOULD ENABLE YOUTH TO SEEK A PATTERN OF LIFE COHERENT IN ITS MATERIAL, INTELLECTUAL AND MORAL DIMENSIONS. IT PURSUES ITS AIMS THROUGH PARTICIPATORY ACTION RESEARCH IN URBAN NEIGHBORHOODS AND RURAL TOWNS ACROSS CALIFORNIA.</MissionDesc>
      <SignificantNewProgramSrvcInd>0</SignificantNewProgramSrvcInd>
      <SignificantChangeInd>0</SignificantChangeInd>
      <ExpenseAmt>133825</ExpenseAmt>
      <GrantAmt>133825</GrantAmt>
      <RevenueAmt>0</RevenueAmt>
      <Desc>INTERNSHIP PROGRAMOVER THE COURSE OF 2024, CDRI ENGAGED 43 HIGH SCHOOL AND COLLEGE YOUTH IN ITS YEAR-LONG INTERNSHIP PROGRAM. THE PROGRAM AIMS TO RAISE CAPACITY IN YOUNG PEOPLE TO CONTRIBUTE MEANINGFULLY TO THE PROGRESS AND DEVELOPMENT OF THEIR COMMUNITIES. INTERNS RECEIVE TRAINING, MENTORSHIP, AND A SCHOLARSHIP WHILE ENGAGED IN ACTION-RESEARCH IN THEIR COMMUNITIES. DURING 2024, INTERNS DEVELOPED CAPACITY BY OFFERING ACADEMIC TUTORING TO MIDDLE SCHOOL STUDENTS.</Desc>
      <ProgSrvcAccomActy2Grp>
        <ExpenseAmt>24920</ExpenseAmt>
        <GrantAmt>15800</GrantAmt>
        <RevenueAmt>0</RevenueAmt>
        <Desc>SUMMER PROGRAMSDURING THE SUMMER OF 2024, CDRI HOSTED MIDDLE SCHOOL SUMMER PROGRAMS IN THREE CITIES: SAN DIEGO, PASADENA, AND SAN PABLO. A TOTAL OF 129 MIDDLE SCHOOL AND ELEMENTARY SCHOOL STUDENTS PARTICIPATED. ADDITIONALLY, 63 HIGH SCHOOL AND COLLEGE-AGE YOUTH WERE TRAINED AND ENGAGED AS TUTORS AND COORDINATORS OF THE SUMMER PROGRAMS. THE TOTAL PROGRAM HOURS ACROSS THE THREE SITES WAS 274 HOURS. PARTICIPANTS STRENGTHENED LANGUAGE AND MATH ABILITIES THROUGH STUDY; THEY PLAYED SPORTS AND LEARNED CRAFTS. THE PROGRAM WAS OFFERED FREE OF CHARGE AND TARGETED UNDER-SERVED NEIGHBORHOODS IN LARGE URBAN CENTERS. THE ACADEMIC TUTORS WERE YOUTH FROM THESE SAME NEIGHBORHOODS. THEY WERE GIVEN SMALL STIPENDS.</Desc>
      </ProgSrvcAccomActy2Grp>
      <ProgSrvcAccomActy3Grp>
        <ExpenseAmt>33040</ExpenseAmt>
        <GrantAmt>0</GrantAmt>
        <RevenueAmt>0</RevenueAmt>
        <Desc>ACADEMIC TUTORINGCDRI OFFERS ACADEMIC TUTORING TO MIDDLE SCHOOL STUDENTS TO ENHANCE THEIR INTELLECTUAL ABILITIES AND ADDRESS EDUCATIONAL ACHIEVEMENT GAPS ASSOCIATED WITH SOCIO-ECONOMIC STATUS. DURING 2024, 145 STUDENTS PARTICIPATED IN CDRI TUTORING IN SAN DIEGO, PASADENA, AND SAN PABLO. TUTORING TOOK PLACE MULTIPLE DAYS PER WEEK ON SCHOOL GROUNDS AND AT COMMUNITY CENTERS.</Desc>
      </ProgSrvcAccomActy3Grp>
