      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>PART I, LINE 2:</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>COHERENT DEVELOPMENT RESEARCH INSTITUTE PROVIDES SCHOLARSHIPS AND STIPENDS TO INDIVIDUALS PURSUING A DEGREE IN HIGHER EDUCATION OR IN THEIR FINAL YEAR OF HIGH SCHOOL WHO ARE PARTICIPATING IN ITS INTERNSHIP PROGRAM. EACH RECIPIENT IS ASSIGNED A MENTOR WHO OVERSEES AND GUIDES THEIR PARTICIPATION IN THE INTERNSHIP PROGRAM OVER THE COURSE OF THE YEAR. MENTORS ARE SUPERVISED BY A PROGRAM COORDINATOR WHO FOLLOWS THE PROGRESS OF ALL RECIPIENTS AND ADDRESSES CHALLENGES AND ANY VIOLATIONS TO PROGRAM REQUIREMENTS. FUNDS ARE PROVIDED DIRECTLY TO RECIPIENTS. IF AN INDIVIDUAL FAILS TO FULFILL THE REQUIREMENTS OF THE FUNDING, EVEN AFTER MULTIPLE INTERVENTIONS ON THE PART OF THE MENTOR AND COORDINATOR, THE FUNDING CAN BE SUSPENDED SUBJECT TO RESOLUTION OF THE BOARD OF DIRECTORS.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
    </IRS990ScheduleI>
    <IRS990ScheduleO documentId="RetDoc1044400001">
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART VI, SECTION A, LINE 8B</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THERE ARE NO SUCH COMMITTEES WITH AUTHORITY TO ACT ON BEHALF OF THE BOARD.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART VI, SECTION B, LINE 11B</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>A COMPLETE COPY OF THE FORM 990, INCLUDING ALL SCHEDULES, IS DISTRIBUTED TO ALL MEMBERS OF THE GOVERNING BODY PRIOR TO FILING. BOARD MEMBERS ARE GIVEN AN OPPORTUNITY TO REVIEW THE DOCUMENT AND PROVIDE FEEDBACK DURING A BOARD MEETING OR BY EMAIL BEFORE SUBMISSION.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART VI, SECTION B, LINE 12C</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE ORGANIZATION'S CONFLICT OF INTEREST POLICY COVERS ITS DIRECTORS, OFFICERS, EMPLOYEES, AND VOLUNTEERS. EACH PERSON SUBJECT TO THIS POLICY SHALL ANNUALLY SIGN A STATEMENT ON THE CONFLICT OF INTEREST DISCLOSURE FORM OR SUCH OTHER FORM AS THE BOARD ADOPTS, WHICH AT A MINIMUM AFFIRMS THAT SUCH PERSON: HAS RECEIVED A COPY OF THE POLICY; HAS READ AND UNDERSTANDS THE POLICY; HAS AGREED TO COMPLY WITH THE POLICY; AND UNDERSTANDS THE CORPORATION IS CHARITABLE AND IN ORDER TO MAINTAIN ITS FEDERAL TAX EXEMPTION IT MUST ENGAGE PRIMARILY IN ACTIVITIES WHICH ACCOMPLISH ONE OR MORE OF ITS TAX-EXEMPT PURPOSES. IN ADDITION, INTERESTED PERSONS SHALL MAKE AN ANNUAL DISCLOSURE OF ON-GOING RELATIONSHIPS AND INTERESTS THAT MAY PRESENT A CONFLICT OF INTEREST. DISCLOSURES SHOULD ADDRESS CURRENT AFFILIATIONS, AS WELL AS PAST AFFILIATIONS FOR THE PRIOR TWO YEARS. CONFLICT OF INTEREST DISCLOSURE FORMS WILL BE SUBMITTED TO THE PRESIDENT ANNUALLY, AND WHEN APPROPRIATE, AT OR PRIOR TO ACTION ON RELEVANT BUSINESS TRANSACTIONS. THE BOARD REVIEWS AND MAKES DETERMINATIONS ON ANY POTENTIAL CONFLICT OF INTEREST. INDIVIDUALS WITH A PERCEIVED CONFLICT OF INTEREST ARE REQUIRED TO LEAVE THE MEETING DURING DISCUSSION AND VOTING UPON TRANSACTIONS OR ARRANGEMENTS INVOLVING SUCH CONFLICTS.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART VI, SECTION C, LINE 19</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE ORGANIZATION'S GOVERNING DOCUMENTS, CONFLICT OF INTEREST POLICY, AND FINANCIAL STATEMENTS ARE ALL MADE AVAILABLE TO THE PUBLIC UPON REQUEST.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
